From a Tragedy of the Commons perspective:
Investing heavily in large farms maximizes short-term returns but accelerates depletion of shared resources, reducing long-term system sustainability.
Investing in small farms with technology reduces pressure on the commons, distributes production, and improves long-term resilience, even if short-term returns are lower.
Conclusion: Ontario should prioritize funding technology for small farms, or at minimum shift funding criteria to reduce pressure on shared resources.
Because in this system, the goal is not just maximizing output today—it is protecting the commons that all future production depends on.